md('# 21. Interpretation\n\nThe reproduced rates are route-weighted synthetic-proxy signals. Payload 0% does not remove capacity from general EVRP models; range 64.4% is not a real failure rate; geographic access is not availability; charging assistance does not prove SOC feasibility; smaller width does not imply practical advantage. Representation choices can add variables, penalties, auxiliaries, depth, and compilation overhead.')
md('# 22. Limitations and Threats to Validity\n\n**Construct:** proxies are not operational routes; width is not total cost. **Internal:** seeds, KMeans, depot selection, 1.25 multiplier, service-time assumptions, and missing charger attributes. **External:** Tokyo/public-data/vehicle assumptions may not generalize. **Reproducibility:** dynamic APIs, vehicle URLs, environment differences, and slide-only circuit values.')
